# What `gcloud builds submit` (deploy/cloudrun.sh) uploads: only what the Dockerfile copies, so a
# .env, .state/ or research/ never leaves this machine. Same syntax as .gitignore
# (https://cloud.google.com/sdk/gcloud/reference/topic/gcloudignore): exclude every top-level
# entry, then re-include the ones the build needs. Keep it in step with .dockerignore.
/*
!/Dockerfile
!/.dockerignore
!/pyproject.toml
!/uv.lock
!/README.md
!/LICENSE
!/tephra/
!/data/
!/docs/
/docs/*
!/docs/backtest/
!/deploy/
/deploy/*
!/deploy/cloudbuild.yaml
**/__pycache__
# data/replay/<case>/raw stays in: REPLAY in the image serves those recorded files.
